================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

The following third-party tools are required to build or run portions of
Nucleor. They are not bundled with this distribution; users obtain them
independently from their respective vendors.

LLVM (clang, lld) — Required.
  License: Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
  URL: https://llvm.org/
  Used as: native code generation and linking back-end. The
  `nucleor_llvm_rt.c` runtime emits LLVM IR which is compiled by clang.

CUDA Toolkit (nvcc) — Optional.
  License: NVIDIA proprietary
  URL: https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-downloads
  Used as: optional GPU code generation for `stdlib/runtime/cuda_rt.cu`
  and `stdlib/runtime/taylor_gpu_rt.cu`. Nucleor programs that do not use
  GPU runtimes do not require CUDA.

Rust toolchain (cargo, rustc) — Optional.
  License: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  URL: https://www.rust-lang.org/
  Used as: optional builder for `stdlib/rods/rust_bridge`, a static
  library that exposes Rust's `regex` crate and other utilities to
  Nucleor programs via C ABI. Nucleor programs that do not import
  `stdlib/rods/rust.nr` do not require Rust.

================================================================================
RUST BRIDGE — TRANSITIVE DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

When `stdlib/rods/rust_bridge` is built (via `cargo build --release`),
the following crates are pulled from crates.io and statically linked into
`nucleor_rust_bridge.lib`. Their licenses apply to the resulting binary:

  regex (MIT OR Apache-2.0)        https://github.com/rust-lang/regex
  aho-corasick (MIT OR Unlicense)  https://github.com/BurntSushi/aho-corasick
  memchr (MIT OR Unlicense)        https://github.com/BurntSushi/memchr

These crates are not bundled with this distribution; they are downloaded
by cargo at build time.
